1b67963c-150b-43f1-8e05-0a96b27766d1,FLEET_MANAGER,FLEET_MANAGER,PRIVACY_POLICY,or,1.0.0,Fleet Manager Privacy Policy,"<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang=""en"">
<head>
  <meta charset=""utf-8"">
  <meta name=""viewport"" content=""width=device-width, initial-scale=1"">
  <title>Fleet Manager Privacy Policy</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light; --text: #11202f; --secondary: #5b6b7c; --muted: #8b9aaa; --accent: #f475d0; --wash: #fdecf8; --ink: #3d0a2c; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
    body { margin: 0; background: #fff; color: var(--secondary); font: 15px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, ""Segoe UI"", Roboto, ""Helvetica Neue"", Arial, sans-serif; }
    main { width: 100%; max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px 18px 28px; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; color: var(--text); font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.3; }
    h2 { margin: 26px 0 8px; color: var(--text); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.35; }
    p { margin: 0 0 13px; }
    strong { color: var(--text); }
    .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
    .notice { margin: 18px 0; padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--wash); color: var(--ink); font-size: 13.5px; }
    a { color: #b63891; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    @media (max-width: 380px) { main { padding: 16px 14px 24px; } }
  </style>
</head>
<body><p role=""note"" class=""legal-translation-review"">[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: English placeholder for Odia (or). Translate this entire document and verify client details before publication.]</p>
<main>
  <h1>Fleet Manager Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class=""meta"">EVsEye Fleet Manager App | Fleet operator: {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}<br>Draft version: 1.0.0 | Effective date: to be assigned at publication</p>
  <p class=""notice""><strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: Confirm data categories, purposes, providers, retention, contacts, and legal approval before publication.]</strong></p>
  <h2>1. Who uses the information</h2>
  <p>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} decides how Fleet Manager account and operational information is used to assign work, supervise fleet activity, review rider and vehicle records, and handle incidents. EV Spares India Pvt Ltd operates the EVsEye platform and decides how platform security, technical support, and service diagnostics information is used. <strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: confirm this division of responsibility and the contact for each organisation.]</strong></p>
  <h2>2. Information handled in the App</h2>
  <p>The App may handle the Fleet Manager's registered mobile number, name, role, assigned hubs, authentication and device security records, actions taken in operational workflows, notes, documents or photographs the manager submits, support requests, and audit records. The manager may also view rider, vehicle, payment, and verification information within assigned permissions. <strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: confirm which of these categories are live, whether phone location or camera access is used, and whether any further information is collected.]</strong></p>
  <h2>3. Why it is used</h2>
  <p>Information is used to authenticate the manager, apply assigned permissions, show relevant work, record and audit operational decisions, coordinate fleet and rider operations, investigate incidents, secure the platform, and provide support. Access to rider information must be limited to authorised work. <strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: confirm each actual purpose and its applicable legal basis before publication.]</strong></p>
  <h2>4. Sharing and service providers</h2>
  <p>Authorised {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} personnel and authorised EV Spares support personnel may access records according to their responsibilities. Service providers may process limited information to deliver hosting, authentication messages, document storage, or operational services. <strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: list the live cloud region, SMS/email, maps, payments, verification, analytics, and support providers; identify any processing or access outside India.]</strong></p>
  <h2>5. Retention and security</h2>
  <p>Access is restricted by role and the platform records significant actions. {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} and EV Spares apply technical and organisational controls to protect information. Records are retained according to the approved category-specific schedule and legal requirements. <strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: state actual retention periods and deletion triggers for account, access, audit, operational, uploaded evidence, payment, and support records; verify the deletion process.]</strong></p>
  <h2>6. Choices, requests, and concerns</h2>
  <p>A Fleet Manager can ask the relevant organisation about access, correction, or other requests concerning their own information through the contacts below. Operational records may need to remain accurate and available where required for legitimate operations or law. <strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: confirm request channels, grievance contact, and response process.]</strong></p>
  <h2>7. Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>Material updates will be published as a new dated version in the App. {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} privacy contact: <strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: name, email, and postal address]</strong>. EV Spares platform contact: <strong>office@evsparesindia.com</strong>. Contact details and the effective date must be verified before publication.</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
",t,,2026-10-12 20:39:50.413,2026-10-12 20:39:50.413
1c6b8fa2-e4f2-410b-a71e-a6c938ee66d7,RIDER,RIDER,TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS,ur,1.0.0,Rider Terms & Conditions,"<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang=""en"">
<head>
  <meta charset=""utf-8"">
  <meta name=""viewport"" content=""width=device-width, initial-scale=1"">
  <title>Rider Terms &amp; Conditions</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --text: #11202f;
      --text-secondary: #5b6b7c;
      --muted: #8b9aaa;
      --accent: #f475d0;
      --wash: #fdecf8;
      --ink: #3d0a2c;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html {
      -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 20px 18px 28px;
      background: #ffffff;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      font: 15px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, ""Segoe UI"", Roboto, ""Helvetica Neue"", Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    .updated {
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 13px;
    }

    .notice {
      margin: 0 0 20px;
      padding: 12px 14px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: var(--wash);
      color: var(--ink);
      font-size: 13.5px;
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 22px 0 8px;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.35;
    }

    h2 span {
      margin-right: 6px;
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    p {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
    }

    ul {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      padding-left: 20px;
    }

    li {
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }

    strong {
      color: var(--text);
    }

    h1 { margin: 0 0 4px; color: var(--text); font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.3; }
    .operator { margin: 0 0 16px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
</style>
</head>
<body><p role=""note"" class=""legal-translation-review"">[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: English placeholder for Urdu (ur). Translate this entire document and verify client details before publication.]</p><p><strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: verify every operational, provider, contact, and retention statement for this client; remove this marker only after legal review]</strong></p>
  <h1>Rider Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
  <p class=""operator"">EVsEye Rider App | Fleet Operator: {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}</p>
  <h2><span>1.</span>Definitions and parties</h2>
  <p>“Platform” means the EVsEye Rider App and supporting technology operated by {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}. “Fleet Operator” means {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}, the entity responsible for the vehicle and rider-facing rental/service arrangement. “Rider” means the individual using the App. Identify the actual contracting entities and their roles before publishing.</p>
  <h2><span>2.</span>Eligibility and onboarding</h2>
  <p>Riders must be at least 18 years old, legally eligible to use the assigned vehicle, and hold a valid licence whenever required. Riders must provide accurate mobile, identity, address, licence and other onboarding details and update changes promptly. Approval and vehicle allocation may depend on verification and operator policies.</p>
  <h2><span>3.</span>Account access and security</h2>
  <p>Access may use a registered mobile number and OTP. Riders must safeguard their devices and report suspected unauthorized access. Account access is personal and must not be sold or transferred.</p>
  <h2><span>4.</span>Services and operator relationship</h2>
  <p>The App supports onboarding, verification, vehicle allocation, hubs, rentals, wallets, payments, maintenance reporting, referrals, training and support where enabled. Availability varies by Fleet Operator, city and subscribed package. The Fleet Operator, not the technology provider merely by operating the App, is responsible for the vehicle rental contract unless explicitly stated otherwise.</p>
  <h2><span>5.</span>Vehicle use and safety</h2>
  <p>Follow traffic laws, safety requirements, vehicle capacity limits, manufacturer guidance and Fleet Operator instructions. Do not lend, sublet, tamper with, modify or use a vehicle or battery for unauthorized purposes. Report accidents, theft, damage, battery issues and breakdowns promptly.</p>
  <h2><span>6.</span>Charges, rate cards and deposits</h2>
  <p>Applicable onboarding fees, rentals, penalties, taxes, refundable deposits, deductions and billing cycles must be shown before acceptance or transaction. Location, vehicle age/category and plan may affect prices only where disclosed in the applicable rate card. A deposit is not automatically forfeited and any deductions must be itemized under the signed rental agreement.</p>
  <h2><span>7.</span>Wallet, payments and mandates</h2>
  <p>Wallet balances, credits, refunds, failed payments and adjustments are displayed in the App where offered. Payment gateways and mandate providers may process payments. UPI AutoPay or eNACH is optional unless clearly disclosed as a condition of a particular rental product; separate, revocable mandate authorization and provider rules apply. No debit beyond a valid authorization is permitted.</p>
  <h2><span>8.</span>Location and connected vehicle information</h2>
  <p>Where vehicles are GPS/IoT enabled, trip, vehicle status, location and safety events may be processed as described in the Privacy Policy. Device or app location permissions must be explained in context. Do not claim tracking only occurs during shifts unless the deployed hardware and operations actually enforce this.</p>
  <h2><span>9.</span>Referrals, rewards and training</h2>
  <p>Referral rewards, self-submission bonuses and training are governed by campaign-specific rules shown in the App, including eligibility, validation, expiry, fraud controls and payout timing. Rewards may be reversed for proven abuse subject to applicable law.</p>
  <h2><span>10.</span>Prohibited activity</h2>
  <p>Do not submit forged documents, impersonate another person, manipulate GPS/odometer/telematics, misuse payment systems, compromise accounts, harass others or use services unlawfully.</p>
  <h2><span>11.</span>Suspension and termination</h2>
  <p>Access may be restricted for safety, fraud, material breach, legal requirements or unpaid dues, with notice and an opportunity to respond where appropriate. On exit, return any allocated vehicle and equipment and complete an itemized settlement. Statutory rights and lawful dispute remedies remain unaffected.</p>
  <h2><span>12.</span>Availability and liability</h2>
  <p>Service features may be interrupted for maintenance, network failures or external events. Nothing excludes liability or consumer rights that cannot lawfully be excluded. Any agreed limitation of liability must be reviewed for fairness and enforceability.</p>
  <h2><span>13.</span>Updates and disputes</h2>
  <p>Material changes will be communicated before taking effect when required. Changes do not retroactively alter an accepted rental contract without appropriate consent. Indian law applies, subject to mandatory consumer protections and legally competent courts/tribunals.</p>
  <h2><span>14.</span>Contact and notices</h2>
  <p>Fleet Operator: {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}, [CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: client registered address], [CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: client support email], [CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: client support phone]. Platform support: office@evsparesindia.com, +91-9871675222. Grievance contact: [CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: client grievance officer], office@evsparesindia.com, [CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: client registered address]. Notices may be sent by in-app message, SMS or registered email, subject to applicable law.</p>
  <h2>Effective date and version</h2>
  <p>Effective date: 01 October 2026. Version: 1.0.0. The Fleet Operator and Platform will retain the version accepted by each Rider.</p>
</body>
</html>
",t,,2026-10-12 20:39:50.522,2026-10-12 20:39:50.522
1ffdd99f-01fc-422e-8afb-f942a68b0203,FLEET_MANAGER,FLEET_MANAGER,TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS,mr,1.0.0,Fleet Manager Terms & Conditions,"<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang=""en"">
<head>
  <meta charset=""utf-8"">
  <meta name=""viewport"" content=""width=device-width, initial-scale=1"">
  <title>Fleet Manager Terms &amp; Conditions</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light; --text: #11202f; --secondary: #5b6b7c; --muted: #8b9aaa; --accent: #f475d0; --wash: #fdecf8; --ink: #3d0a2c; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
    body { margin: 0; background: #fff; color: var(--secondary); font: 15px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, ""Segoe UI"", Roboto, ""Helvetica Neue"", Arial, sans-serif; }
    main { width: 100%; max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px 18px 28px; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; color: var(--text); font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.3; }
    h2 { margin: 26px 0 8px; color: var(--text); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.35; }
    p { margin: 0 0 13px; }
    strong { color: var(--text); }
    .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
    .notice { margin: 18px 0; padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--wash); color: var(--ink); font-size: 13.5px; }
    a { color: #b63891; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    @media (max-width: 380px) { main { padding: 16px 14px 24px; } }
  </style>
</head>
<body><p role=""note"" class=""legal-translation-review"">[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: English placeholder for Marathi (mr). Translate this entire document and verify client details before publication.]</p>
<main>
  <h1>Fleet Manager Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
  <p class=""meta"">EVsEye Fleet Manager App | Fleet operator: {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}<br>Draft version: 1.0.0 | Effective date: to be assigned at publication</p>
  <p class=""notice""><strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: Confirm client legal name, contacts, authority and escalation rules, enabled financial actions, and legal approval before publication.]</strong></p>
  <h2>1. Who these terms apply to</h2>
  <p>These terms govern access to the EVsEye Fleet Manager App by an individual authorised by {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} to manage its fleet operations. “{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}” means the fleet operator identified in the applicable employment or service arrangement. “EV Spares” means EV Spares India Pvt Ltd, which provides the EVsEye platform. “You” means the authorised Fleet Manager. These terms govern use of the App; your employment, compensation, and authority to act for {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} are governed by your separate arrangement with {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}.</p>
  <h2>2. Account and authority</h2>
  <p>Use only the account assigned to you. Keep your phone, OTPs, and access credentials secure; do not share them or allow another person to work under your identity. Your access is limited to the locations, riders, vehicles, and actions assigned by {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}. Inform {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} promptly if your device, account, or credentials are lost or compromised. {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} may change your role or withdraw access when your duties change.</p>
  <h2>3. Operational records and decisions</h2>
  <p>Enter accurate, timely information about rider onboarding, identity and document review, vehicle inspection, allocation, handover, return, incidents, maintenance, and other enabled workflows. Check original evidence where {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s procedure requires it. Do not approve, reject, change, or delete a record without a legitimate operational reason. Record the reason for significant decisions when the App asks for one. A status shown by the App is an operational record, not a substitute for any required physical check, signed agreement, or legal approval.</p>
  <h2>4. Vehicles, riders, and safety</h2>
  <p>Follow {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s safety, inspection, allocation, and escalation procedures. Do not release an unsafe or ineligible vehicle, override a failed check, or knowingly allocate a vehicle to a person who has not met applicable requirements. Report accidents, theft, damage, battery issues, breakdowns, and suspected misuse promptly through the designated process. Use rider and vehicle information only to carry out authorised duties.</p>
  <h2>5. Documents, photographs, and verification</h2>
  <p>Upload only relevant and genuine documents and photographs. Do not alter evidence to misrepresent its content. Where the App offers third-party verification, treat the result as one part of the applicable review process and follow {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s procedure for exceptions. Do not download, copy, forward, or store rider identity documents outside approved systems unless {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} expressly authorises it and a lawful purpose requires it.</p>
  <h2>6. Payments and financial records</h2>
  <p>If your role includes deposits, rent, refunds, wallet adjustments, or invoices, enter transactions accurately and use only approved payment channels. Do not request payment to a personal account, promise an undisclosed fee waiver, or make an unapproved adjustment. The App may record who performed an action and when. Any authority to collect or approve money comes from {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s separate policy and assigned permissions.</p>
  <h2>7. Confidentiality and personal information</h2>
  <p>Rider, staff, vehicle, financial, and business information visible in the App is confidential. Access only records needed for your assigned work; do not use them for personal purposes or share them with unauthorised people. Follow {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s privacy and data-handling instructions and the Fleet Manager Privacy Policy presented separately in the App. Report an accidental disclosure or suspected data incident promptly. This clause does not prevent a disclosure required by law or a protected report to a competent authority.</p>
  <h2>8. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Do not impersonate another user, submit false information, manipulate location or vehicle data, bypass permissions, probe the service for vulnerabilities, introduce harmful software, or use the App for harassment or unlawful activity. Do not use automated access or extract bulk records without written authorisation. Use App features only for the purposes made available to your role.</p>
  <h2>9. Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>Features depend on {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s configuration and may change as its operations change. Connectivity, device, and third-party failures can interrupt access. Keep an appropriate manual escalation route for urgent safety decisions. Material changes to these terms will be presented for acceptance when required; the App records the version and time accepted.</p>
  <h2>10. Suspension and end of access</h2>
  <p>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} may suspend or end your access because of a role change, security concern, suspected misuse, or the end of your arrangement with {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}. Return company devices and records and stop using copied information when access ends, subject to lawful retention and reporting obligations. Suspected wrongdoing should be reviewed under {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s applicable process; an App restriction alone is not a final employment decision.</p>
  <h2>11. Responsibility and disputes</h2>
  <p>These terms do not remove rights or obligations that cannot legally be excluded. Your separate agreement with {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} controls employment or service matters. Indian law applies to these App terms, subject to mandatory law and the jurisdiction of legally competent courts or tribunals. Concerns about fleet operations should first be raised with {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}; platform access or technical concerns may be raised with EV Spares.</p>
  <h2>12. Contacts</h2>
  <p>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} fleet operations: <strong>[confirm legal name, postal address, authorised email, and support phone before publication]</strong>.</p>
  <p>EV Spares platform support: <strong>office@evsparesindia.com</strong>.</p>
  <p>Notices may be sent through the App or to a contact address you provide, subject to applicable law.</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
