3e6a69cd-0cba-4ce4-8354-c325cddb4882,RIDER,RIDER,PRIVACY_CONSENT,bn,1.0.0,গোপনীয়তা বিষয়ক বিজ্ঞপ্তি ও সম্মতিপত্র,"<!doctype html>
<html lang=""bn"">
<head>
  <meta charset=""utf-8"">
  <meta name=""viewport"" content=""width=device-width, initial-scale=1"">
  <title>গোপনীয়তা বিষয়ক বিজ্ঞপ্তি ও সম্মতিপত্র</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light; --text: #11202f; --secondary: #5b6b7c; --muted: #8b9aaa; --accent: #f475d0; --wash: #fdecf8; --ink: #3d0a2c; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
    body { margin: 0; background: #fff; color: var(--secondary); font: 15px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, ""Segoe UI"", Roboto, ""Helvetica Neue"", Arial, sans-serif; }
    main { width: 100%; max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px 18px 28px; }
    .hero { margin-bottom: 16px; }
    .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 8px; color: var(--accent); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; color: var(--text); font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.3; }
    h2 { margin: 26px 0 8px; color: var(--text); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.35; }
    p, ul { margin: 0 0 13px; }
    ul { padding-left: 20px; }
    li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
    strong { color: var(--text); }
    .muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
    a { color: #b63891; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .callout { margin-top: 24px; padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--wash); color: var(--ink); }
    .callout h2 { margin-top: 0; }
    @media (max-width: 380px) { main { padding: 16px 14px 24px; } }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <!-- [CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: Resolve every Bengali client-review note before publication.] -->
  <header class=""hero"">
    <p class=""eyebrow"">এগিয়ে যাওয়ার আগে</p>
    <h1>গোপনীয়তা বিষয়ক বিজ্ঞপ্তি ও সম্মতিপত্র</h1>
    <p>'ডিজিটাল ব্যক্তিগত তথ্য সুরক্ষা আইন ২০২৩' (Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023)-এর অধীনে ব্যক্তিগত তথ্য সংগ্রহের জন্য সম্মতিপত্র।</p>
    <p class=""muted"">[ক্লায়েন্টের পর্যালোচনা প্রয়োজন: প্রকাশের আগে ডেটা ফিডুসিয়ারি (data fiduciary), DPO-এর যোগাযোগের তথ্য, প্রতিটি ডেটার ধরন, উৎস এবং শেয়ার করার উদ্দেশ্য নিশ্চিত করুন।]</p>
  </header>

  <section class=""card"" aria-labelledby=""purpose"">
    <h2 id=""purpose"">তথ্য সংগ্রহের উদ্দেশ্য</h2>
    <p>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}-এর প্ল্যাটফর্মে রাইডারদের যুক্ত করা (onboard) যাতে তারা পরিষেবা গ্রহণ করতে পারেন এবং পরবর্তী লেনদেনগুলো সম্পন্ন করা সহজ হয়।</p>
  </section>

  <section class=""card"" aria-labelledby=""details"">
    <h2 id=""details"">সংগৃহীত তথ্যের ধরন</h2>
    <p>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} নিম্নলিখিত ব্যক্তিগত তথ্য সংগ্রহ করবে:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>পরিচয় সংক্রান্ত তথ্য (PAN, নাম, বাবার নাম এবং জন্ম তারিখ)।</li>
      <li>ঠিকানার প্রমাণপত্র (আধার কার্ড, ড্রাইভিং লাইসেন্স, পাসপোর্ট বা অন্য কোনো সরকারিভাবে বৈধ নথি)।</li>
      <li>যোগাযোগের তথ্য (ইমেল ঠিকানা এবং ফোন নম্বর)।</li>
      <li>আর্থিক তথ্য (নিট সম্পদ বা আয়ের বিবরণী), যদি প্রযোজ্য হয়। [ক্লায়েন্টের পর্যালোচনা প্রয়োজন: এই তথ্য সংগ্রহ করা হচ্ছে কি না তা নিশ্চিত করুন।]</li>
      <li>ক্রেডিট সংক্রান্ত তথ্য। [ক্লায়েন্টের পর্যালোচনা প্রয়োজন: এই তথ্য সংগ্রহ করা হচ্ছে কি না তা নিশ্চিত করুন এবং সংশ্লিষ্ট উদ্দেশ্য উল্লেখ করুন।]</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class=""card"" aria-labelledby=""sources"">
    <h2 id=""sources"">তথ্য সংগ্রহের উৎস</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>NSDL। [ক্লায়েন্টের পর্যালোচনা প্রয়োজন: NSDL একটি সক্রিয় উৎস কি না তা যাচাই করুন।]</li>
      <li>সরকার, সংবিধিবদ্ধ বা নিয়ন্ত্রক কর্তৃপক্ষের দ্বারা পরিচালিত ডেটাবেস। [ক্লায়েন্টের পর্যালোচনা প্রয়োজন: প্রযোজ্য উৎসগুলো চিহ্নিত করুন।]</li>
      <li>অনবোর্ডিংকারী সংস্থা বা ব্যবহারকারী।</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class=""card"" aria-labelledby=""sharing"">
    <h2 id=""sharing"">তথ্য শেয়ার করা</h2>
    <p>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}-এর সংবিধিবদ্ধ, নিয়ন্ত্রক ও সরকারি কর্তৃপক্ষের সাথে; ব্যবসায়িক ও পরিচালনগত কাজের জন্য নিযুক্ত পরিষেবা প্রদানকারীদের সাথে; এবং কোম্পানির পরিষেবা প্রদানে সহায়তাকারী পক্ষগুলোর সাথে তথ্য শেয়ার করার অনুমোদন রয়েছে। [ক্লায়েন্টের পর্যালোচনা প্রয়োজন: প্রতিটি বিভাগের জন্য গ্রহীতা, উদ্দেশ্য এবং আইনি ভিত্তি নিশ্চিত করুন।]</p>
  </section>

  <section class=""card"" aria-labelledby=""choice"">
    <h2 id=""choice"">ডেটা প্রিন্সিপাল বা তথ্য প্রদানকারীর অধিকার</h2>
    <p>আপনার সম্মতিতে প্রক্রিয়াজাত করা ব্যক্তিগত তথ্য সংশোধন, সম্পূর্ণকরণ, হালনাগাদ এবং মুছে ফেলার জন্য আপনি অনুরোধ করতে পারেন এবং যেকোনো সময় আপনার সম্মতি প্রত্যাহার করতে পারেন। এই অধিকারগুলো প্রয়োগ করতে, কোম্পানির সাথে যোগাযোগ করুন [ক্লায়েন্টের পর্যালোচনা প্রয়োজন: যাচাইকৃত DPO বা অভিযোগ সংক্রান্ত ইমেল ঠিকানাটি এখানে দিন]-এ।</p>
    <p>সম্মতি প্রত্যাহারের অনুরোধ সত্ত্বেও, কোম্পানি প্রযোজ্য আইন অনুযায়ী নির্ধারিত সময়সীমা পর্যন্ত এবং সম্মতি প্রত্যাহারের আগে শুরু হওয়া লেনদেনের প্রয়োজনে তথ্য সংরক্ষণ করতে পারে। কোনো অভিযোগ বা অসন্তোষের বিষয়ে যোগাযোগ করুন [ক্লায়েন্টের পর্যালোচনা প্রয়োজন: অভিযোগ জানানোর যাচাইকৃত যোগাযোগের মাধ্যম]-এ। কোনো অভিযোগের সুরাহা না হলে, প্রযোজ্য আইন অনুযায়ী বিষয়টি ‘ডেটা প্রোটেকশন বোর্ড’-এর কাছে উত্থাপন করা যেতে পারে। [ক্লায়েন্টের পর্যালোচনা প্রয়োজন: প্রকাশের আগে মূল ফর্মে থাকা ৯০-দিনের মধ্যে অভিযোগ উত্থাপন সংক্রান্ত ভাষাটি যাচাই করুন।]</p>
  </section>

  <section class=""card callout"" aria-labelledby=""agreement"">
    <h2 id=""agreement"">ঘোষণা</h2>
    <p>আমি ঘোষণা করছি যে, আমি এই সম্মতিপত্রের বিষয়বস্তু বুঝেছি এবং ‘ডেটা প্রিন্সিপাল’ (যাঁর ডেটা বা তথ্য) হিসেবে এতে সম্মত হচ্ছি। অ্যাপের ভেতরে সম্মতিসূচক চেকবক্সটি মূল ফর্মে থাকা কাগজের স্বাক্ষর, নাম এবং পদবির স্থানগুলোর বিকল্প হিসেবে কাজ করবে। [ক্লায়েন্টের পর্যালোচনা প্রয়োজন: ইলেকট্রনিক সম্মতির ভাষাটি অনুমোদন করুন।]</p>
  </section>
</main>
</body>
</html>
",t,,2026-10-12 20:39:50.124,2026-10-12 21:26:58.763
452e1211-92de-4bb1-8e62-9cd21877371a,FLEET_MANAGER,FLEET_MANAGER,TERMS_AND_CONDITIONS,bn,1.0.0,Fleet Manager Terms & Conditions,"<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang=""en"">
<head>
  <meta charset=""utf-8"">
  <meta name=""viewport"" content=""width=device-width, initial-scale=1"">
  <title>Fleet Manager Terms &amp; Conditions</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light; --text: #11202f; --secondary: #5b6b7c; --muted: #8b9aaa; --accent: #f475d0; --wash: #fdecf8; --ink: #3d0a2c; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
    body { margin: 0; background: #fff; color: var(--secondary); font: 15px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, ""Segoe UI"", Roboto, ""Helvetica Neue"", Arial, sans-serif; }
    main { width: 100%; max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px 18px 28px; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; color: var(--text); font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.3; }
    h2 { margin: 26px 0 8px; color: var(--text); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.35; }
    p { margin: 0 0 13px; }
    strong { color: var(--text); }
    .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
    .notice { margin: 18px 0; padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--wash); color: var(--ink); font-size: 13.5px; }
    a { color: #b63891; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    @media (max-width: 380px) { main { padding: 16px 14px 24px; } }
  </style>
</head>
<body><p role=""note"" class=""legal-translation-review"">[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: English placeholder for Bengali (bn). Translate this entire document and verify client details before publication.]</p>
<main>
  <h1>Fleet Manager Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
  <p class=""meta"">EVsEye Fleet Manager App | Fleet operator: {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}<br>Draft version: 1.0.0 | Effective date: to be assigned at publication</p>
  <p class=""notice""><strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: Confirm client legal name, contacts, authority and escalation rules, enabled financial actions, and legal approval before publication.]</strong></p>
  <h2>1. Who these terms apply to</h2>
  <p>These terms govern access to the EVsEye Fleet Manager App by an individual authorised by {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} to manage its fleet operations. “{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}” means the fleet operator identified in the applicable employment or service arrangement. “EV Spares” means EV Spares India Pvt Ltd, which provides the EVsEye platform. “You” means the authorised Fleet Manager. These terms govern use of the App; your employment, compensation, and authority to act for {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} are governed by your separate arrangement with {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}.</p>
  <h2>2. Account and authority</h2>
  <p>Use only the account assigned to you. Keep your phone, OTPs, and access credentials secure; do not share them or allow another person to work under your identity. Your access is limited to the locations, riders, vehicles, and actions assigned by {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}. Inform {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} promptly if your device, account, or credentials are lost or compromised. {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} may change your role or withdraw access when your duties change.</p>
  <h2>3. Operational records and decisions</h2>
  <p>Enter accurate, timely information about rider onboarding, identity and document review, vehicle inspection, allocation, handover, return, incidents, maintenance, and other enabled workflows. Check original evidence where {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s procedure requires it. Do not approve, reject, change, or delete a record without a legitimate operational reason. Record the reason for significant decisions when the App asks for one. A status shown by the App is an operational record, not a substitute for any required physical check, signed agreement, or legal approval.</p>
  <h2>4. Vehicles, riders, and safety</h2>
  <p>Follow {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s safety, inspection, allocation, and escalation procedures. Do not release an unsafe or ineligible vehicle, override a failed check, or knowingly allocate a vehicle to a person who has not met applicable requirements. Report accidents, theft, damage, battery issues, breakdowns, and suspected misuse promptly through the designated process. Use rider and vehicle information only to carry out authorised duties.</p>
  <h2>5. Documents, photographs, and verification</h2>
  <p>Upload only relevant and genuine documents and photographs. Do not alter evidence to misrepresent its content. Where the App offers third-party verification, treat the result as one part of the applicable review process and follow {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s procedure for exceptions. Do not download, copy, forward, or store rider identity documents outside approved systems unless {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} expressly authorises it and a lawful purpose requires it.</p>
  <h2>6. Payments and financial records</h2>
  <p>If your role includes deposits, rent, refunds, wallet adjustments, or invoices, enter transactions accurately and use only approved payment channels. Do not request payment to a personal account, promise an undisclosed fee waiver, or make an unapproved adjustment. The App may record who performed an action and when. Any authority to collect or approve money comes from {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s separate policy and assigned permissions.</p>
  <h2>7. Confidentiality and personal information</h2>
  <p>Rider, staff, vehicle, financial, and business information visible in the App is confidential. Access only records needed for your assigned work; do not use them for personal purposes or share them with unauthorised people. Follow {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s privacy and data-handling instructions and the Fleet Manager Privacy Policy presented separately in the App. Report an accidental disclosure or suspected data incident promptly. This clause does not prevent a disclosure required by law or a protected report to a competent authority.</p>
  <h2>8. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Do not impersonate another user, submit false information, manipulate location or vehicle data, bypass permissions, probe the service for vulnerabilities, introduce harmful software, or use the App for harassment or unlawful activity. Do not use automated access or extract bulk records without written authorisation. Use App features only for the purposes made available to your role.</p>
  <h2>9. Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>Features depend on {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s configuration and may change as its operations change. Connectivity, device, and third-party failures can interrupt access. Keep an appropriate manual escalation route for urgent safety decisions. Material changes to these terms will be presented for acceptance when required; the App records the version and time accepted.</p>
  <h2>10. Suspension and end of access</h2>
  <p>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} may suspend or end your access because of a role change, security concern, suspected misuse, or the end of your arrangement with {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}. Return company devices and records and stop using copied information when access ends, subject to lawful retention and reporting obligations. Suspected wrongdoing should be reviewed under {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s applicable process; an App restriction alone is not a final employment decision.</p>
  <h2>11. Responsibility and disputes</h2>
  <p>These terms do not remove rights or obligations that cannot legally be excluded. Your separate agreement with {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} controls employment or service matters. Indian law applies to these App terms, subject to mandatory law and the jurisdiction of legally competent courts or tribunals. Concerns about fleet operations should first be raised with {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}; platform access or technical concerns may be raised with EV Spares.</p>
  <h2>12. Contacts</h2>
  <p>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} fleet operations: <strong>[confirm legal name, postal address, authorised email, and support phone before publication]</strong>.</p>
  <p>EV Spares platform support: <strong>office@evsparesindia.com</strong>.</p>
  <p>Notices may be sent through the App or to a contact address you provide, subject to applicable law.</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
",t,,2026-10-12 20:39:50.131,2026-10-12 20:39:50.131
49181bce-89a0-40ce-abcf-1e141d87d948,RIDER,RIDER,PRIVACY_POLICY,or,1.0.0,Rider Privacy Policy,"<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang=""en"">
<head>
  <meta charset=""utf-8"">
  <meta name=""viewport"" content=""width=device-width, initial-scale=1"">
  <title>Rider Privacy Policy</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light; --text: #11202f; --secondary: #5b6b7c; --muted: #8b9aaa; --accent: #f475d0; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
    body { margin: 0; padding: 20px 18px 28px; background: #fff; color: var(--secondary); font: 15px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, ""Segoe UI"", Roboto, ""Helvetica Neue"", Arial, sans-serif; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; color: var(--text); font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.3; }
    h2 { margin: 26px 0 8px; color: var(--text); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.35; }
    p, ul { margin: 0 0 13px; }
    ul { padding-left: 20px; }
    li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
    a { color: #b63891; }
    .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body><p role=""note"" class=""legal-translation-review"">[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: English placeholder for Odia (or). Translate this entire document and verify client details before publication.]</p><p><strong>[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: verify every operational, provider, contact, and retention statement for this client; remove this marker only after legal review]</strong></p>
  <h1>Rider Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class=""meta"">EVsEye Rider App | Fleet Operator: {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}<br>Effective date: 01 October 2026 | Version: 1.0.0</p>
  <p>This Policy explains how personal information is used when a Rider uses the EVsEye Rider App for {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}. It applies to the features made available to that Rider. If a feature is not enabled, the information needed only for that feature is not requested through it.</p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible for your information</h2>
  <p>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}, [CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: client location], decides how Rider information is used for onboarding, identity and eligibility checks, vehicle allocation, payments, and fleet operations. EV Spares India Pvt Ltd independently decides how information is used for EVsEye account security, platform support, and service analytics. EV Spares also operates the EVsEye platform on {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s behalf for {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s Rider operations. Contact details for both organisations are in section 14.</p>

  <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
  <p>Depending on the enabled service, information may include your name, mobile number, date of birth, address, photograph, emergency or reference contacts, driving licence, onboarding answers, vehicle allocation and usage, payment and wallet transactions, support requests, training completion, and referral records. Identity checks may use PAN, Aadhaar-related verification information, and bank-account verification information where requested in the App. The specific fields required for a feature are shown when you provide them.</p>

  <h2>3. Identity verification and Aadhaar</h2>
  <p>Where an identity check is required, verification information is shared with Sandbox, our KYC service provider, for the requested check. The platform stores verification results and masked identifiers needed to administer the check; identity numbers are not displayed publicly. Aadhaar verification, if enabled, is used only for the disclosed identity-check purpose. Riders may ask what verification information is held about them using the contact details below.</p>

  <h2>4. Location, vehicle IoT, and app permissions</h2>
  <p>If you choose to use nearby-hub features and grant location permission, the App uses your phone's location while the App is in use to find relevant hubs. The App does not collect phone location in the background for {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} Riders. A vehicle with GPS or IoT hardware can independently transmit its location, battery, speed, ignition, and other vehicle-status or safety events. That hardware can operate when the App is closed and may continue operating outside an active shift while powered. Vehicle IoT information is used for fleet operations, safety, maintenance, and theft or incident investigation.</p>

  <h2>5. Face verification</h2>
  <p>Face matching and liveness verification are not active for {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} Riders. If either is introduced, we will provide a separate explanation of the images and results collected, the provider, retention, and available choices before use.</p>

  <h2>6. Why we use information</h2>
  <p>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} uses Rider information to create and manage Rider accounts, verify identity and eligibility, allocate and administer vehicles, manage rent, deposits, invoices and payments, provide training and support, maintain vehicle safety, investigate incidents and suspected fraud, and meet applicable legal obligations. EV Spares uses information to secure accounts and the EVsEye service, respond to platform support requests, troubleshoot and improve service reliability, and analyse service use. Referral information is used only where a referral feature is enabled.</p>

  <h2>7. Notice, permissions, and choices</h2>
  <p>We present the information requested for each feature when it is collected. Where consent is required, it is requested for the stated purpose and may be withdrawn as applicable under law by contacting us. Optional phone-location permission can be denied or changed in your device settings; nearby-hub results may then be unavailable or less relevant. Withdrawal of information necessary to provide a requested Rider service may limit that service, subject to legal and contractual obligations.</p>

  <h2>8. Sharing and service providers</h2>
  <p>Information is shared only as needed for the purposes above with authorised {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} personnel and EV Spares platform personnel, and with service providers under appropriate access controls. Current or applicable providers include Sandbox for enabled KYC checks, Razorpay and Cashfree for payment processing, MSG91 for email delivery, and Amazon Web Services for hosting. Where a feature is enabled, an SMS provider may process a phone number and one-time code, and a map or routing service may process a location used for a route or nearby-hub search. A provider receives only the information needed for its task. Information may also be disclosed to insurers, maintenance partners, or authorities where needed for a service, claim, safety matter, or legal requirement.</p>

  <h2>9. Client separation and access</h2>
  <p>The platform separates {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}'s operational data from other fleet operators' data. Access is limited by user role and the operational task. EV Spares staff may access information for approved support, security, maintenance, or legal purposes; access is not represented as zero. Requests for emergency or legally compelled access are handled according to the applicable process.</p>

  <h2>10. Storage, retention, and security</h2>
  <p>Core platform information is hosted on Amazon Web Services infrastructure in India. The exact AWS region can vary by deployment. A service provider's processing location may differ; information about a specific provider can be requested using the contacts below. Access controls, audit records, and technical safeguards are used to protect information according to the service configuration.</p>
  <p>KYC and identity-check records, vehicle GPS/IoT history, and support records are retained for up to one year from collection, unless a longer period is necessary for an active legal hold, investigation, dispute, or applicable law. Payment, invoice, tax, and accounting records are retained for the period required by applicable law; where GST record-keeping rules apply, this is generally at least 72 months from the due date of the annual return for the relevant year, and longer where proceedings require it. Account and active vehicle-allocation information is retained while needed to provide and administer the Rider service, then reviewed for deletion or de-identification subject to legal and dispute requirements. Retention and deletion are administered by the responsible teams.</p>

  <h2>11. Your rights and grievances</h2>
  <p>Subject to applicable law, you may request information about processing, correction or updating of inaccurate information, erasure where appropriate, withdrawal of consent where applicable, and resolution of a grievance. Send a request to the privacy contact in section 14. We may verify your identity before acting and may retain information when a legal obligation, live dispute, or other lawful ground requires it. Any applicable nomination right may be exercised through the same contact.</p>

  <h2>12. Age and eligibility</h2>
  <p>The Rider service is intended for adults aged 18 or older. {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} does not knowingly onboard a minor as a vehicle Rider. If information about a minor is submitted in error, contact us so it can be reviewed and corrected or deleted as appropriate.</p>

  <h2>13. Security incidents and policy changes</h2>
  <p>The responsible organisation will assess suspected security incidents and provide notices when required by applicable law. Material changes to this Policy will be communicated through the App or another appropriate channel. The current version and effective date will be shown with the Policy; renewed consent will be sought when required.</p>

  <h2>14. Contact details</h2>
  <p>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} (Rider operations), [CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: client location]: <a href=""mailto:[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: client support email]"">[CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: client support email]</a>, [CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: client support phone]. Privacy and grievance contact: [CLIENT_REVIEW_REQUIRED: client grievance officer], at the {{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}} contact above. EV Spares India Pvt Ltd (EVsEye platform): <a href=""mailto:office@evsparesindia.com"">office@evsparesindia.com</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
",t,,2026-10-12 20:39:50.38,2026-10-12 20:39:50.38
